==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|satet}}, {{m|enm|satyt}}, {{m|enm|saded}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|sate|ed}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# In a state of complete and thorough [[satisfaction]]; having one’s [[appetite]] fully satisfied, by having [[enough]] of something.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello Q1|I|iii|19|When ſhee is '''ſated''' with his body, ſhee will finde the error of her choyce;}}
# [[quelled|Quelled]] of thirst or hunger.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|satiate}} / [[satiated]]
* {{l|en|satisfied}}
* {{l|en|full}} ''(informal, as pertains to food)''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|satedness}}
* {{l|en|unsated}}

